# Helfy eCommerce — AI Engineering Rules
# Cursor reads this file automatically on every request.
# Canonical long-form rules live in ai-blueprint/guidelines/ and ai-blueprint/capabilities/.
# This file is a hard-constraint summary — never override these in generated code.

# ============================================================
# REPO LAYOUT — MONOREPO (npm workspaces)
# ============================================================
# Root
#   frontend/    React app (Vite)
#   backend/     Express API
#   shared/      End-to-end TypeScript types + Zod schemas
#   database/    migrations/ + seeds/ (Drizzle-generated SQL)
#   ai-blueprint/ initial.md + guidelines/ + capabilities/
# NEVER put app code at the repo root.
# NEVER create a separate repo for frontend or backend.

## STACK (NON-NEGOTIABLE)

### Frontend
- Runtime: React 19 + Vite 6 + TypeScript 5 (strict)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS v4 + shadcn/ui (new-york style) — use shadcn CSS variables for all colors, NEVER hardcode hex or Tailwind palette colors directly
- Animation: Framer Motion
- Icons: Lucide React
- Routing: React Router v7
- State: Zustand (authStore, cartStore, uiStore)
- Server state / caching: TanStack Query v5
- Forms: React Hook Form + Zod
- HTTP client: Axios (configured instance at frontend/src/api/client.ts)
- Shared types: imported from `shared` workspace, NOT re-declared in frontend

### Backend
- Runtime: Node 20 LTS + Express 4 + TypeScript 5 (strict)
- ORM: Drizzle ORM (mysql2 driver) — schema files in backend/src/db/schema/
- Migrations: Drizzle Kit — output to database/migrations/
- Database: MySQL 8 (local dev via Docker, see docker-compose.yml)
- Auth: JWT — access token (15m, in-memory) + refresh token (7d, httpOnly cookie)
- Password hashing: argon2 (NOT bcrypt)
- Validation: Zod (every route input validated before controller)
- Logger: pino
- Security: helmet, cors (whitelist), express-rate-limit
- Env validation: Zod schema in backend/src/config/env.ts — fail fast on startup if vars missing
- Shared types: imported from `shared` workspace

### Shared workspace (shared/src/)
- All TypeScript interfaces and Zod schemas that are used by BOTH frontend and backend live here
- Frontend and backend import from `@helfy/shared`
- Never duplicate type definitions between packages

### Database
- Engine: MySQL 8 with utf8mb4_unicode_ci
- ORM: Drizzle — define schema in backend/src/db/schema/, generate migrations with `npm run db:generate`, apply with `npm run db:migrate`
- Seeds: database/seeds/*.seed.ts — run with `npm run db:seed`
- NEVER write raw SQL in application code — use Drizzle query builder
- NEVER use SELECT * — always select only needed columns

### Testing
- Frontend: Vitest + Testing Library
- Backend: Vitest + supertest
- Tests live alongside source in __tests__/ or *.test.ts files

## FOLDER STRUCTURE — ALWAYS FOLLOW THIS

### Frontend (frontend/src/)
```
api/
  client.ts          ← Axios instance (base URL, interceptors, token refresh)
  auth.api.ts
  products.api.ts
  cart.api.ts
  orders.api.ts
components/
  ui/                ← shadcn primitives only (button, card, dialog, input…)
  layout/            ← Header, Footer, MobileNav, Container, PageShell
  features/          ← ProductCard, CartLine, CheckoutStepper, OrderTimeline…
hooks/               ← useAuth, useCart, useDebounce, useMediaQuery
store/               ← Zustand stores (authStore.ts, cartStore.ts, uiStore.ts)
pages/               ← route-level components (one file per route)
routes/              ← route definitions, ProtectedRoute, router config
lib/                 ← cn(), formatPrice(), motion variants, validators
styles/              ← globals.css (Tailwind v4 @import + @theme tokens)
types/               ← frontend-only types (not shared with backend)
```

### Backend (backend/src/)
```
modules/             ← domain-driven, one folder per bounded context
  auth/              ← routes.ts, controller.ts, service.ts, repository.ts, validators.ts, types.ts
  users/
  products/
  categories/
  cart/
  orders/
  reviews/
db/
  client.ts          ← Drizzle client + mysql2 connection pool
  schema/            ← users.ts, products.ts, orders.ts … (one file per table group)
middleware/          ← auth.middleware.ts, error.middleware.ts, validate.middleware.ts, rateLimit.ts
config/              ← env.ts (Zod-validated), constants.ts
utils/               ← AppError.ts, asyncHandler.ts, jwt.ts, logger.ts
types/               ← express.d.ts (req.user augmentation)
app.ts               ← Express app composition (middleware + routes)
server.ts            ← HTTP server bootstrap (port, signals)
```

## CODING STANDARDS

### TypeScript
- Strict mode ON (`"strict": true` in tsconfig) for ALL packages
- No `any` — use `unknown` and narrow with type guards or Zod `.parse()`
- Prefer `as const` objects over TypeScript enums for shared FE/BE constants
- Use TypeScript enums only when required by a library
- All API responses must match the typed response envelope (see below)
- Import shared types from `@helfy/shared`, never re-declare them

### Naming Conventions
- React components / pages: PascalCase (`ProductCard.tsx`, `CatalogPage.tsx`)
- All other files: kebab-case (`auth.service.ts`, `use-cart.ts`, `api-contracts.md`)
- Variables / functions: camelCase
- Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE
- DB tables / columns: snake_case (Drizzle handles TS mapping with `casing: 'camelCase'`)
- Env vars: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE (`JWT_ACCESS_SECRET`, `DATABASE_HOST`)
- Zod schemas: suffixed with `Schema` (`loginSchema`, `productSchema`)

### Error Handling
- Backend: all errors go through centralized `error.middleware.ts` — NEVER send stack traces to client in production
- All async route handlers wrapped with `asyncHandler` utility — no try/catch boilerplate in controllers
- Use `AppError` class (extends Error) with `statusCode` and `code` fields
- Frontend: React Error Boundaries on every page, toast notifications for API errors
- HTTP status codes: 400 validation, 401 unauthenticated, 403 forbidden, 404 not found, 409 conflict, 422 unprocessable, 500 server error

### API Response Envelope (ALWAYS use this shape)
```typescript
// Success
{ success: true, data: T, message?: string }

// Error
{ success: false, error: string, code: string, details?: unknown }

// Paginated list
{ success: true, data: T[], pagination: { page: number, limit: number, total: number, totalPages: number } }
```

### Security Rules
- Passwords: argon2 hashing (NOT bcrypt, NOT SHA)
- JWT secrets: minimum 64 characters, validated at startup by env.ts
- All inputs validated with Zod before reaching controller — use `validate.middleware.ts`
- ORM only — NEVER raw SQL in application code
- CORS: whitelist `CORS_ORIGINS` env var only
- Auth rate limit: 10 requests per 15 min window on /auth routes
- General rate limit: 100 requests per 15 min window on all routes
- httpOnly + Secure cookies for refresh tokens in production (`COOKIE_SECURE=true`)

### Performance
- Images: always specify width + height attributes, use `loading="lazy"` outside viewport
- Lists: always paginate, default limit 20, max 100
- Drizzle queries: always select only needed columns — never `.select()` with no fields specified
- MySQL FULLTEXT index on product name + description for catalog search
- Debounce search inputs at 300ms

## UI/UX RULES
- Color: use shadcn CSS custom properties (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `text-primary`, etc.) — NEVER raw Tailwind palette colors like `bg-slate-900` or `text-indigo-500`
- Dark premium feel is achieved via the shadcn `@theme` token overrides in globals.css, not inline classes
- Every interactive element must have visible hover + focus-visible states
- Loading states: skeleton screens (not spinner-only)
- Empty states: helpful message + action button — never a blank white box
- Mobile-first responsive: design for 375px first, then scale up
- Smooth page transitions: Framer Motion `AnimatePresence` on route changes
- Framer Motion variants: define in `lib/motion.ts`, import — never inline animation objects

## FEATURE SCOPE — NEVER SKIP THESE

### Authentication
- Email + password signup / login
- JWT access token (15m, stored in memory / TanStack Query cache)
- Refresh token (7d, httpOnly cookie)
- Refresh token rotation on every use (old token invalidated immediately)
- Logout: clear cookie + invalidate refresh token in DB
- Logout-all-devices: invalidate all refresh tokens for user
- Protected routes: redirect to login if no valid token

### Product Catalog
- Full-text search (MySQL FULLTEXT on name + description)
- Filter by category, price range, brand, min rating
- Sort by price asc/desc, newest, popularity
- Pagination (20 per page default)
- URL-driven filter/sort state (query params) — filters survive page refresh
- Debounced search input (300ms)

### Product Detail Page
- Image gallery with thumbnail navigation
- Size / color variant stubs (structure only, no inventory tracking)
- Customer reviews (create, list)
- Related products section
- Add to cart with Framer Motion feedback

### Cart
- Persistent for authenticated users (stored in DB, `carts` + `cart_items`)
- Guest cart: `session_id` (UUID) in localStorage + `cart_items` keyed to session
- Merge on login: dedup by `product_id`, sum quantities, keep lowest price snapshot
- Line item: update quantity, remove item — optimistic UI with rollback
- Cart badge count in header updates instantly

### Checkout (4-step stepper)
1. Shipping — address form (saved addresses or new)
2. Payment — mocked (input fields present, no live charge)
3. Review — order summary before submit
4. Confirmation — order ID, estimated delivery
- Payment is mocked behind a `PaymentService` interface (Stripe plug-in documented as future work)

### Account
- Profile: edit name, email, password
- Addresses: create, edit, delete, set default
- Order history: paginated list with status badge
- Order detail: line items, shipping address, status timeline
- All account routes are protected

### Admin (optional stretch goal — build after core features)
- Basic product management: add, edit, delete products
- Mark as out of stock

## DOCKER & LOCAL DEV
- MySQL 8 + Adminer run via `docker-compose.yml` at repo root
- Start DB: `npm run db:up` (from root)
- Backend reads `DATABASE_URL` from backend/.env
- Never hardcode DB credentials — always read from env

## AI BLUEPRINT WORKFLOW
- The graded "engine" lives in ai-blueprint/
- ai-blueprint/initial.md is the bootstrap prompt for regenerating the entire project
- ai-blueprint/guidelines/ contains long-form cross-cutting rules
- ai-blueprint/capabilities/ contains per-domain building blocks
- This .cursorrules file is a summary of those documents — ai-blueprint/ is the source of truth

## COMMIT STYLE
